inals.\n     - R2.3: File type keyword to LS_COLORS code mapping table (22 keywords: DIR=di, LINK=ln, EXEC=ex, FIFO=pi, SOCK=so, BLK=bd, CHR=cd, ORPHAN=or, SETUID=su, SETGID=sg, STICKY=st, OTHER_WRITABLE=ow, STICKY_OTHER_WRITABLE=tw, CAPABILITY=ca, MULTIHARDLINK=mh, NORMAL=no, FILE=fi, RESET=rs, MISSING=mi, LEFT=lc, RIGHT=rc, END=ec). Extensions with \".\" prefix get \"*\" prepended.\n     - R2.4: File argument reading, stdin via \"-\", built-in defaults when no file given, defaults must match gdircolors --print-database\n     - R2.5: \"-\" filename reads from stdin\n\n   - **cmd/dircolors/main.go** (to be modified, currently ~508 lines)\n     - Already contains substantial R2 implementation from the R1 task\n     - `keywordToCode` map (lines 17-41): Maps all 22 file type keywords to LS_COLORS codes\n     - `ignoredKeywords` map (lines 43-47): COLOR, OPTIONS, EIGHTBIT\n     - `parseDatabase()` function (lines 155-241): Parses database format with comments, TERM/COLORTERM entries, keyword values, extensions\n     - `termMatches()` function (lines 243-260): Uses filepath.Match for glob matching against TERM/COLORTERM env vars\n     - `defaultDatabase` constant (lines 263-508): Full GNU default database including TERM entries, COLORTERM, file type keywords, and extension mappings\n     - `detectShell()` function (lines 146-153): Auto-detects shell from SHELL env var\n     - `main()` function (lines 57-143): Handles flag parsing, file/stdin reading, output formatting\n\n   - **cmd/dircolors/dircolors_test.go** (to be modified, currently 124 lines)\n     - Uses testutils.BuildBinary and exec.LookPath(\"gdircolors\")\n     - Has `discardStderr` normalizer for error output tests\n     - 22 existing test cases covering: shell flags (-b, --sh, --bourne-shell, -c, --csh, --c-shell), auto-detection (bash/tcsh/csh/zsh), mutual exclusivity (last flag wins), print database (-p, --print-database), error cases (extra operand with -p), custom database from stdin, empty database, com